# dp_exchange_robinhood — environment variable template.
#
# This is the ONLY .env file that is committed. `.gitignore` carries
# `.env*` / `!.env.sample`; every other .env is yours and stays local.
#
#     cp .env.sample .env
#
# Secrets live in .env files and nowhere else. There is no `config/*.secret.exs` and no
# Vault layer.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This package needs no venue credentials, and that is deliberate
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# It does NOT handle authentication. The host does, and the host holds the key —
# Robinhood Crypto issues an Ed25519 API key plus a base64 32-byte private-key seed, and
# obtaining, storing and rotating that pair is the host's decision, not this package's.
# This package signs one request with credentials a caller hands it per call; it never
# obtains, stores, refreshes or reads one.
#
# So there is no Robinhood API key here, even though EVERY endpoint on this venue needs
# one — there is no public surface at all (docs/reference/robinhood/endpoint-inventory.md).
# Tier-1 tests use in-process fakes and a stubbed HTTP transport, which is why they need no
# credential; there are no tier-2 tests here, because a tier-2 test would need one. A
# credential sitting in this repo would have nothing to do, and an unused credential is a
# liability with no upside.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Publishing
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Organisation key. CI publishes with the org secret; this is only for publishing by hand.
HEX_API_KEY=<your-hex-api-key>
